    "title": "ShopRite Easter hours for Monmouth, Ocean county stores",
    "text": "April 3, 2026, 9:01 a.m. ETPlanning a last-minute holiday feast?Don't worry, be hoppy! There's a ShopRite in your area that will be open.The supermarket giant has 180 locations across 142 towns and cities in New Jersey. And, we have rounded up the holiday hours for 16 stores for shoppers in a shell.So in case you need to head out on Easter Sunday for butter or bread, some ShopRite locations across Monmouth and Ocean counties will be open.Shop Rite locations in Monmouth, Ocean CountyHours can vary by store. We recommend using the ShopRite store locator or calling your local shop to confirm their final closing time before you head out.Aberdeen: 7 a. m. to 5 p.m.; 732-566-9111Bricktown: 6 a. m. to 4 p.m.; 732-477-7906Fischer Bay: 6 a. m. to 4 p.m; 732-270-8833Freehold: 6 a. m. to 4 p.m.; 732-462-3120Hazlet: 6 a. m. to 4 p.m.; 732-264-4110Howell: 6 a. m. to 4 p.m.; 848-299-0080Jackson: 6 a. m. to 4 p.m.; 732-886-7009Kings Commons: 6 a. m. to 5 p.m.; 732-671-9444Lacey: 6 a. m. to 4 p.m.; 609-693-1152Manchester: 6 a. m. to 4 p.m.; 732-657-0700Marlboro: 6 a. m. to 4 p.m.; 732-617-0404Neptune: 7 a. m. to 4 p.m.; 732-775-4250Route 37: 6 a. m. to 4 p.m732-286-4500Shrewsbury: 6 a. m. to 4 p.m.; 732-380-0411Wall Township: 6 a. m. to 6 p.m.; 732-292-9780West Long Branch: 6 a. m. to 4 p.m.; 732-542-5222",
